<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 9-month coconut oil export down 41 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippine 9-month coconut oil export down 41 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine coconut oil exports fell by 41 percent to 601,415 tonnes in the first nine months of the year from the year-ago level of 1,025,461 tonnes, the United Coconut Associations of the Philippines said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>For the month of September alone, coconut oil exports dropped to about 65,000 tonnes, against 94,744 tonnes in September 1995.</p>
<p>Traders blamed the decline on a series of typhoons which devastated coconut growing areas in Bicol in the central Philippines late last year.</p>
<p>Tight supplies of coconut oil are expected to ease next year, they said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, Fax 817-62-67</p>
</text>
